# Bulk data and build products. Notebooks are tracked deliberately -- the original
# `*.ip*` rule is why the 2017 modelling work was never committed and is now lost.
#
# `*.pkl` and `*.h5` stay ignored on purpose: model weights reach the web app host by
# scp, not through git. That is what lost `FinalModel.pkl` in 2017, so the difference
# now is that the artifact is one command to rebuild (`cli train`) and carries its own
# provenance -- `cli describe --model FinalModel.pkl` says which commit and which
# corpus produced the file on the box. Do not "fix" this by committing weights.
*.csv
*.json
*.pkl
*.h5

# Test fixtures must be tracked despite the patterns above.
!tests/fixtures/**

# Cached Basketball-Reference pages: ~250 KB each, ~160 MB over the corpus, and
# refetchable in about 35 minutes. See rebounding/data/bref.py.
data/bref/

# Build products. `cli.py build` regenerates these from the tracking archives and
# the page cache; only the inputs belong in git.
*.parquet

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
